SUMMARY:HKSTP x PCIM Asia 2026 - power electronics expo\, hiring + networki
 ng (Golden Egg)
DESCRIPTION:HKSTP x PCIM Asia 2026. REGISTRATION CONFIRMED\, confirmation n
 o. PA265. NOON ARRIVAL AGREED: Candice Chen (Messe Frankfurt) replied 13 O
 ct 14:55 HKT\, verbatim\, "No problem. You can check in and get your badge
  at noon upon arrival. We will keep your seat for the Talent Engagement se
 ssion." OFFICIAL PARTICIPANT NOTICE arrived 14 Oct 12:37 HKT: check-in 09:
 30-10:00 at G/F Building 10W\, badge issued on site against your registere
 d full name or the confirmation number\, badge must be worn in the auditor
 ium and exhibition area and is NON-TRANSFERABLE\, event hours 10:00-17:00\
 , bilingual English and Mandarin. The notice also warns seating is first-c
 ome-first-served\, so noon is permission to arrive\, not a guaranteed seat
 \; carry Candice's reply and answer from that thread if the desk queries i
 t. HOW TO GET THERE (notice wording): MTR to University Station then bus 2
 72K to Hong Kong Science Park\, or minibus 27 from MTR Sha Tin Station\; b
 y car via Tolo Highway with over 1500 paid parking spaces on site includin
 g EV charging. Place: Charles K. Kao Auditorium (the Golden Egg)\, Hong Ko
 ng Science Park\, Pak Shek Kok\, Sha Tin\; registration and badge collecti
 on at G/F\, Building 10W\, directly under the auditorium. OFFICIAL PROGRAM
 ME: 09:30-10:00 registration\; 10:00-10:10 opening remarks (Mr Richard Li\
 , Messe Frankfurt HK)\; 10:10-10:30 keynote Gaoqing Song\, Mitsubishi Elec
 tric\; 10:30-10:50 keynote Kim Wang\, Infineon\; 10:50-11:10 keynote Liyua
 n Ran\, Bosch\; 11:10-11:30 keynote Joe Guo\, STMicroelectronics\; 11:30-1
 2:10 panel discussion with joint universities\; 12:10-12:20 HKSTP CEO spee
 ch\; 12:20-12:30 HKSTP and PCIM partnership signing\; 12:30-14:30 TALENT E
 NGAGEMENT (the session the seat is held for)\; 14:30-14:45 keynote Devin G
 u\, Murata\; 14:45-15:00 keynote Tim Wong\, SMC Automation\; 15:00-15:15 k
 eynote Barry Mok\, VTech\; 15:15-16:15 business pitching\; 16:15-17:00 boo
 th communication and networking. Recording presentations is prohibited wit
 hout consent\; personal photos for non-commercial use only. Notice PDF fil
 ed in the vault beside the event note and in Downloads. Earlier research k
 ept for completeness: other routes also serve the park (272A\, 272P\, 272S
 \, 272X\, 43P\, 43S\, 74D\, 74P\, 82C\, 263A\, 271B\, 907D\, 96\, 582)\, a
 nd the free Innocentre shuttle runs mornings and evenings only\, so it doe
 s not help at noon. If coming from home in Pak Shek Kok\, the venue is abo
 ut a 15 minute walk away\, and the MTR plus 272K advice applies to arrival
 s from Sha Tin or University only.
END:VEVENT
