SUMMARY:Kitty Lau - Zoom call (Techathon+ diabetic foot screening project)
DESCRIPTION:Join: https://hkmu.zoom.us/j/92161474365 | Meeting ID: 921 6147
  4365. Hosted from his own HKMU Zoom account, so he is the host and has to
  admit her from the waiting room. Join five minutes early and test mic and
  camera. PURPOSE: decide whether her role for him is bigger and better tha
 n the one GUJIZAI gives him. Nothing gets agreed on the call. THE FIVE QUE
 STIONS THAT DECIDE IT: what would he own end to end and what is the first 
 deliverable; how many hours a week between now and January; who else is on
  the team today and is he the first member or the only engineer; why him s
 pecifically; and what exists today, a working device, a prototype or a des
 ign. THE COMPARISON: role size, who sets technical direction, team maturit
 y, evidence behind the idea, first deliverable, hours, what he gets out of
  it, and risk of the team dissolving. THREE OUTCOMES: stay on GUJIZAI and 
 help from outside her roster, which is rules compatible; switch to her tea
 m, which means telling Kehan first; or decline and keep the relationship. 
 THE RULES, verbatim: each individual member can only participate in only o
 ne team in this edition, so it is a swap, not an addition. BOUNDARIES: exp
 loratory only, no undefined help out role, no spending, no patient facing 
 work on this call. Do not open with GUJIZAI, but answer directly if she ra
 ises the team question. RECORD SIX THINGS: her role and title, who else is
  on the team, what he would own, the first deliverable, hours per week, an
 d what exists today. Full eighteen question checklist is in the vault note
 , Techathon+ Gujizai folder, Kitty Lau - Zoom call prep and questions.
LOCATION:Zoom (online)
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT30M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Kitty Zoom in 30 min - be host, admit her, five decision questi
 ons
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
